<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>PreferenceSpecifiers</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>When on, the hub uses its front camera to recognize enrolled household members. Face data stays on this device. When off, the camera is not used for recognition and everyone gets the guest experience unless a profile is picked by hand.</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<true/>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>face.recognitionEnabled</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Recognize Faces</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSToggleSwitchSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>When the camera cannot confirm that a recognized face is a real person (no depth camera, or the person is too far away), the hub may still switch to that person's layout. Personal content stays locked either way. Turn this off to treat such a face as a guest.</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<true/>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>face.indeterminateLivenessPersonalizes</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Personalize Without Depth Check</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSToggleSwitchSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>On an iPad without Face ID, after the camera recognizes a household member, any fingerprint enrolled on this iPad unlocks that member's personal content until they leave. Touch ID confirms that someone who can unlock this iPad is present, not which person. The iPad passcode is not accepted. Needs Personalize Without Depth Check to be on.</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<true/>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>face.touchIDUnlock</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Unlock with Touch ID</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSToggleSwitchSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>How sure the hub must be before it accepts a face as a household member. Relaxed recognizes people more readily and is more likely to mistake one person for another. Strict does the opposite.</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<string>standard</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>face.matchStrictness</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Match Strictness</string>
			<key>Titles</key>
			<array>
				<string>Relaxed</string>
				<string>Standard</string>
				<string>Strict</string>
			</array>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSMultiValueSpecifier</string>
			<key>Values</key>
			<array>
				<string>relaxed</string>
				<string>standard</string>
				<string>strict</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>How long the hub waits after it stops seeing the recognized person before it locks their profile.</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<integer>3</integer>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>face.lockDelaySeconds</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Lock After Face Is Lost</string>
			<key>Titles</key>
			<array>
				<string>1 second</string>
				<string>3 seconds</string>
				<string>5 seconds</string>
				<string>10 seconds</string>
				<string>30 seconds</string>
			</array>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSMultiValueSpecifier</string>
			<key>Values</key>
			<array>
				<integer>1</integer>
				<integer>3</integer>
				<integer>5</integer>
				<integer>10</integer>
				<integer>30</integer>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>FooterText</key>
			<string>The hub shows the most detail to someone within arm's reach, less at mid range, and the least from across the room. Standard puts arm's reach at about 1 m (3 ft) and across the room at about 2.5 m (8 ft). Closer moves both about a quarter nearer to the screen, and Farther about a third farther away. Distances are estimates.</string>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSGroupSpecifier</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>DefaultValue</key>
			<string>standard</string>
			<key>Key</key>
			<string>face.nearDistance</string>
			<key>Title</key>
			<string>Detail Distance</string>
			<key>Titles</key>
			<array>
				<string>Closer</string>
				<string>Standard</string>
				<string>Farther</string>
			</array>
			<key>Type</key>
			<string>PSMultiValueSpecifier</string>
			<key>Values</key>
			<array>
				<string>closer</string>
				<string>standard</string>
				<string>farther</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>StringsTable</key>
	<string>FaceRecognition</string>
	<key>Title</key>
	<string>Face Recognition</string>
</dict>
</plist>
